cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Urban Auto, please cite it as below. / При использовании модуля просьба ссылаться так:"
title: "Urban Auto: QGIS plugin for annual built-up area maps from Landsat"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kalenov
    given-names: Ruslan
    affiliation: "Russian State Agrarian University – Moscow Timiryazev Agricultural Academy"
version: 5.5.1
date-released: 2026-11-19
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/76458436a-lgtm/urbanauto"
url: "https://github.com/76458436a-lgtm/urbanauto"
abstract: >-
  QGIS Processing plugin that builds a built-up area map for every year of a
  period (e.g. 2000–2025) from a city name or polygon. Training labels are
  derived automatically from open products (GHSL, WSF, ESA WorldCover, JRC GSW,
  OpenStreetMap, Microsoft buildings); summer Landsat composites are classified
  with gradient boosting, the year of built-up appearance is detected, and
  accuracy with 95 % CI is estimated from labelled check points (Olofsson).
keywords:
  - QGIS
  - urban growth
  - built-up area
  - Landsat
  - remote sensing
  - change detection
  - machine learning
